[Term]
id: DOID:0050118
name: encefalitis de La Crosse
alt_id: DOID:10840
def: "A viral infectious disease that results_in inflammation located_in brain, has_material_basis_in La Crosse virus (Orthobunyavirus lacrosseense), which is primarily transmitted_by treehole mosquito (Ochlerotatus triseriatus) but also Asian tiger mosquito (Aedes albopictus) and Asian bush mosquito (Aedes japonicus). The infection has_symptom seizures, has_symptom headache, has_symptom fever, has_symptom coma, and has_symptom paralysis." [url:https\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Crosse_encephalitis, url:https\://www.cdc.gov/la-crosse-encephalitis/about/, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562248/]
subset: DO_infectious_disease_slim
subset: zoonotic_infectious_disease
