id: DOID:0050976
name: spinocerebellar ataxia 27A
alt_id: DOID:0111794
def: "An autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia that is characterized by general cerebellar dysfunction manifest as gait disturbances, ataxia, tremor, dysarthria, and gaze-evoked nystagmus and has_material_basis_in heterozygous mutation in the FGF14 gene on chromosome 13q33. Some patients have heterozygous deletions of chromosome 13q33 affecting the FGF14 and ITGBL1 genes, which may thus be considered a contiguous gene deletion syndrome." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32162847/]
