[Term]
id: DOID:0051091
name: developmental and epileptic encephalopathy 122
def: "A developmental and epileptic encephalopathy that is characterized by infantile hypotonia, severe neurodevelopmental delay, intractable seizures, and distinct dysmorphic features and that has_material_basis_in homozygous mutation in the MDGA2 gene on chromosome 14q21." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41570816/]
xref: MIM:621608
is_a: DOID:0050737 ! enfermedad autosómica recesiva
is_a: DOID:0112202 ! encefalopatía epiléptica y del desarrollo

[Term]
id: DOID:0051092
name: Damseh-Danson neurodevelopmental disorder
def: "An autosomal recessive intellectual developmental disability that is characterized by global developmental delay apparent from infancy and that has_material_basis_in homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the SNX27 gene on chromosome 1q21." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41609011/]
xref: MIM:621591
is_a: DOID:0060308 ! trastorno autosómico recesivo del desarrollo intelectual

[Term]
id: DOID:0051093
name: retinitis pigmentosa 102
def: "A retinitis pigmentosa that is charaterized by onset of night blindness and loss of peripheral vision in adolescence, and eventual reduction in visual acuity with progression of disease and that has_material_basis_in heterozygous mutation in the RNU4-2 gene on chromosome 12q24." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41513982/]
xref: MIM:621560
is_a: DOID:0050736 ! enfermedad autosómica dominante
is_a: DOID:10584 ! retinosis pigmentaria

[Term]
id: DOID:0051094
name: retinitis pigmentosa 103
