name: disostosis frontonasal acromélica
def: "A dysostosis characterized by cranium bifidum, severe hypertelorism, median cleft lip and palate, nasal bifurcation, brachycephaly, large fontanelle, tibial hemimelia, preaxial polydactyly of the feet and brain malformations and that has_material_basis_in heterozygous mutation in the ZSWIM6 gene on chromosome 5q12." [url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15264282]
