[Term]
id: DOID:0060785
name: leucodistrofia desmielinizante autosómica dominante adulta
def: "An adult onset demyelinating leukodystrophy characterized by autonomic abnormalities, pyramidal and cerebellar dysfunction, and symmetric demyelination of the CNS, presenting in the fourth or fifth decade of life, and that has_material_basis_in a heterozygous tandem genomic duplication on chromosome 5q23 that results in an extra copy of the lamin B1 gene (LMNB1), but also alters regulatory sequences that affect expression of other genes." [url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK338165/, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16951681, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19151023]
