name: hormone receptor-positive/HER2-positive breast cancer
def: "A HER2 positive breast cancer characterized by excess HER2 (ERBB2) protein and at least one of the estrogen or progesterone receptors." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22153890/, url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39062682/, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-her2-status.html, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-hormone-receptor-status.html]
is_a: DOID:0060079 ! cáncer de mama con receptores Her2 positivos
is_a: DOID:0070784 ! hormone receptor-positive breast cancer

[Term]
id: DOID:0070780
name: hormone receptor-positive/HER2-negative breast cancer
def: "A HER2 negative breast cancer characterized by at least one of the estrogen or progesterone receptors and the absence of HER2 (EBBR2) protein." [url:https\://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10847323/, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-her2-status.html, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-hormone-receptor-status.html, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25682076]
is_a: DOID:0060080 ! cáncer de mama con receptor Her2 negativo
is_a: DOID:0070784 ! hormone receptor-positive breast cancer

[Term]
id: DOID:0070781
name: HER2-low breast cancer
def: "A breast cancer characterized by low levels of HER2 (EBBR2) protein." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40282933/, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-her2-status.html]
is_a: DOID:1612 ! cáncer de mama

[Term]
id: DOID:0070782
name: HER2-ultralow breast cancer
def: "A breast cancer characterized by very low, but detectable, levels of HER2 (EBBR2) protein." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40282933/, url:https\://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/breast-cancer/understanding-a-breast-cancer-diagnosis/breast-cancer-her2-status.html]
is_a: DOID:1612 ! cáncer de mama

[Term]
id: DOID:0070783
name: idiopathic generalized epilepsy 20
def: "A generalized epilepsy characterized by partial epilepsy, with onset usually early in the first decade of life, that evolves to include complex partial seizures and secondary generalized tonic-clonic seizures associated with focal, and sometimes diffuse, EEG abnormalities that has_material_basis_in compound heterozygous mutation in the ZFHX3 gene on chromosome 16q22." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38508705/]
