[Term]
id: DOID:0081284
name: tumor glioneuronal formador de rosetas
def: "Neoplasia benigna del sistema nervioso central que se caracteriza por la presencia de neurocitos que forman pseudorosetas y astrocitos que contienen fibras de Rosenthal." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36230557/]
subset: DO_cancer_slim
subset: NCIthesaurus
xref: ICDO:9509/1
xref: NCI:C129431
is_a: DOID:0060090 ! neoplasia benigna del sistema nervioso central

[Term]
id: DOID:0081285
name: Tumor glioneuronal mixoide
def: "A central nervous system benign neoplasm that is characterized by a dinucleotide mutation at codon 385 of the PDGFR gene. It usually occurs in the septum pellucidum but has also been described in the corpus callosum and periventricular white matter of the lateral ventricle. It is composed of oligodendrocyte-like cells in a prominent myxoid stroma." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34297434/]
subset: DO_cancer_slim
subset: NCIthesaurus
synonym: "Tumor glioneuronal mixoide" EXACT []
xref: ICDO:9509/1
xref: NCI:C179229
is_a: DOID:0060090 ! neoplasia benigna del sistema nervioso central

[Term]
id: DOID:0081286
name: Tumor embrionario con rosetas multicapa
def: "Tumor embrionario del sistema nervioso central que se caracteriza por la presencia de formación de rosetas multicapa y típicamente la presencia de amplificación de la región C19MC en el cromosoma 19 (19q13.42) o raramente una mutación DICER1." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36451902/]
subset: DO_cancer_slim
subset: NCIthesaurus
synonym: "Tumor embrionario con rosetas multicapa" EXACT []
xref: ICDO:9478/3
