id: DOID:0081432
name: síndrome de microcefalia-micromelia
def: "A syndrome that is characterized by intrauterine growth retardation (IUGR), marked microcephaly, craniosynostosis, and severe malformation of the limbs, especially the arms and that has_material_basis_in homozygous mutation in the DONSON gene on chromosome 21q22. Biallelic mutation in the DONSON gene can also cause microcephaly, short stature, and limb abnormalities, a less severe disorder." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28630177/]
subset: DO_rare_slim
