id: DOID:0110801
name: hereditary sensory and autonomic neuropathy type 9
def: "A hereditary sensory and autonomic neuropathy characterized by global developmental delay, intellectual disability, hypotonia, dysarthria, abnormal gait, hyporeflexia, and central hypoventilation or apnea that has_material_basis_in homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the TECPR2 gene on chromosome 14q32. Additional symptoms due to peripheral neuropathy or autonomic dysfunction are more variable." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33847017/, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK584409/, url:https\://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23176824]
