[Term]
id: DOID:12570
name: glaucoma facolítico
def: "A phacogenic glaucoma that is characterized by acute onset of open-angle glaucoma secondary to a leaking mature or hypermature cataract and has_symptom chronic progressive vision loss with acute onset of pain, redness, and blurry vision. Phacolytic glaucomas are caused by direct obstruction of aqueous outflow pathways from leaking cataractous lens proteins." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30950286/]
xref: ICD9CM:365.51
xref: SNOMEDCT_US_2025_09_01:32893002
xref: UMLS_CUI:C0152137
