[Term]
id: DOID:12571
name: glaucoma facogénico
def: "A glaucoma characterized by glaucomatous optic atrophy secondary to a lens abnormality and has_symptom progressive decreased vision, especially decreased peripheral vision. Phacogenic glaucoma can be caused by cataracts, trauma to the eye, or age-related damage that obstructs aqueous outflow, leading to inappropriately increased intraocular pressure and eventual optic nerve atrophy with associated vision loss." [url:https\://eyewiki.aao.org/Lens_Induced_Glaucomas]
xref: ICD9CM:365.5
xref: SNOMEDCT_US_2025_09_01:84333006
